    "context": "# Goal\nrevenger round 95, attempt 1, lane repo /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin (every path in your task is absolute; the fleet root /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin is NOT your write surface).\nTwo claims are FROZEN at lane commit 6e0bf15fed58f357b7fa0c881371ac7616a116f7 in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-95/claims.md. Read that file in full first; its predicates, counters, kill rules and controls are frozen bytes — never edit them. The frozen r93/r94 instruments (reports/round-93/*, reports/round-94/*) are also frozen bytes — never edit them.\nC1 (coverage, K 11/15 -> 12/15): coverage-map row C10 moves partial -> held, backed by the superseding entry /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/corpus/knowledge/round-95-evidence-ledger-discipline.md (r74-rejected candidate superseded; drift-check rows S500/S501 opened 2026-11-05 with receipts frozen under reports/round-95/quote-receipts/). Counter: reports/round-95/c1_k_admit_counter4.py.\nC2 (calibration): the v4 counter kills the r94-routed NAMED VECTORS (eleven) that the FROZEN r94 v3 counter still passes. Battery: reports/round-95/forge_battery4.py.\n\n# Digest recipe (vote binding)\nThe votes bind sha256 over the entry bytes with every line matching `^\\s*admission-status\\s*:.*$` (case-insensitive) replaced by `admission-status: candidate`. Compute it from the lane root:\nPYTHONUTF8=1 python3 -B -c \"import hashlib,re;t=open('corpus/knowledge/round-95-evidence-ledger-discipline.md',encoding='utf-8').read();n=re.sub(r'(?im)^\\s*admission-status\\s*:.*$','admission-status: candidate',t);print(hashlib.sha256(n.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest())\"\nThe working-tree entry bytes equal the freeze commit's bytes (verify with `git -C /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin show 6e0bf15fed58f357b7fa0c881371ac7616a116f7:corpus/knowledge/round-95-evidence-ledger-discipline.md | sha256sum` vs the file's sha256sum). ExecFrozen's digest.txt carries the same value once it lands.\n\n# Vote file shape (ReviewerGate / ReviewerBlind / CriticR95 only)\nWrite JSON in YOUR wave dir as <yourdir>/vote.json:\n{\"seat\": \"<your exact registry seat name>\", \"role\": \"<your registry role>\", \"candidate_sha256\": \"<digest>\", \"decisions\": {\"Q01\": \"PASS\"|\"n/a\", ..., \"Q17\": ...}, \"notes\": {\"Qxx\": \">=6 tokens containing a Q cross-reference like Q11, for EVERY n/a\"}, \"artifact_path\": \".ufo/waves/round-95/w1/<YourSeat>/<file>\", \"artifact_sha256\": \"<sha256 of that file>\"}\nRules the frozen counter enforces: >=2 accepted votes; seat must be your pinned registry name (no case/space variants); role must equal the pinned registry role (reviewer|critic); >=1 PASS decision; every n/a note >=6 tokens AND contains a Q\\d{2} cross-reference; the artifact is non-empty, distinct per seat, inside YOUR OWN dir .ufo/waves/round-95/w1/<YourSeat>/ after resolution, and its bytes must contain BOTH your seat name and the 64-hex digest string. Write the artifact file first, sha256 it, then the vote.json. ANY malformed vote fails the whole leg, so self-check before you finish.\n\n# Bounds (hard; the sentinel audits this wave)\n- Write ONLY inside your own wave dir /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-95/w1/<YourSeat>/ and your scratch. Seats NEVER edit lane files (corpus/, reports/, SCORECARD, LOG, SKILL, README, PROVINCE, QUALITY, claims), never run git/jj write commands anywhere, never touch the fleet repo, sibling lanes, .ufo/state, .ufo/watchdog.log, or /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokuknow. Read-only seats return findings in their wave dir.\n- Scratch: /fast/scratch/hyaku/revenger-r95/<YourSeat>/ — create with mkdir -p, pass explicitly, DELETE it before you yield (copy receipts into the wave dir first). /tmp only for files under 50 MB; nothing committed may hardcode /tmp. A scratch tree left behind is a self-reported defect.\n- Every seat Python invocation uses `python3 -B` (r94 lesson M5: a seat without -B wrote a .pyc into corpus/; the sentinel audits this).\n- Never mutate host sysctls; never sudo; pacman is PAUSED host-wide (install tools only via uv tool / npx / an official binary into ~/.local/bin; you are authorized, record anything you install).\n- No `agent://all`; you are a leaf (an executor may spawn ONE read-only labrat probe; no other spawns; no swarm).\n- Every `Report:` trailer path in your rendered task is RELATIVE TO /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin — write it at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/<that path>. Network use is limited to the URLs your task names (raw.githubusercontent.com/morluto/rea; github.com/morluto/rea). No other network.\n- Provider errors: report the last error text in your output and stop; do not re-route or retry through other providers.\n\n# Wave facts\nRound shape: ONE v1 wave, 13 seats (band 8-16), attack share 4/13 (>=25%), 1 connector, no residual call. Routing is the operator's task.agentModelOverrides — no model is ever passed. The wave settles when all 13 seats report; the L1 integrates and lands.\n",
